Now I have thoroughly read all three files. Let me synthesize my analysis as the product advocate and produce the required JSON output.

{"agent_id":"agy-product-advocate","role_summary":"Own decision criterion 2: work backwards from a dashboard a user would actually trust and find useful, and state what the schema must carry to make that dashboard viable despite pervasive evidence gaps.","recommendation":"The schema must carry three parallel layers per sensor-axis-crop tuple: (1) a scored evidence band when direct evidence exists, (2) an explicit coverage_status enum exposing WHY no score exists, and (3) a linked qualitative_action from section 9 that replaces the score with actionable prose. A dashboard built on this can show a confident gauge for air temperature on basil, a translucent 'monitoring only' card for humidity with the downy-mildew guidance, and a clearly-grayed 'no evidence' card for CO2 — each with a one-tap drill-down to provenance. The screen is useful because every sensor channel always shows SOMETHING: either a number, a contextual warning, or honest guidance.","why":["A dashboard where 5 of 8 sensor cards say 'unknown' with no follow-up will be abandoned within a week — evidence fidelity without user value is a vanity exercise","The documents already contain rich qualitative guidance (section 9) for every axis where numeric scores fail; the schema must make this guidance as queryable and displayable as a number","Users trust dashboards that explain their own uncertainty — showing a confidence tier (scored/advisory/monitor-only) per card is more credible than hiding gaps or fabricating scores","The evidence-status vocabulary from the gap registry (10 enum values) maps directly to UI states: scored, advisory-with-context, or record-only — this mapping must live in the schema not in frontend code"],"schema_sketch":"-- What the dashboard needs from the knowledge base:\n\nCREATE TABLE crop (\n  crop_id        TEXT PRIMARY KEY,  -- e.g. 'basil'\n  display_name   TEXT NOT NULL,\n  scientific_name TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\nCREATE TABLE sensor_axis (\n  axis_id    TEXT PRIMARY KEY,  -- e.g. 'air_temp', 'air_humidity'\n  unit       TEXT NOT NULL,\n  display_name TEXT NOT NULL\n);\n\n-- Core table: one row per crop × axis × value_type combination\n-- value_type distinguishes optimum / caution / danger / disease_risk / experimental_condition\nCREATE TABLE evidence_band (\n  band_id         INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop_id         TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES crop(crop_id),\n  axis_id         TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sensor_axis(axis_id),\n  value_type      TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(value_type IN (\n    'optimum','caution_low','caution_high','danger_low','danger_high',\n    'disease_risk','experimental_condition')),\n  range_low       REAL,          -- NULL when qualitative-only\n  range_high      REAL,          -- NULL for single-point thresholds\n  unit            TEXT NOT NULL,  -- stored per-band to prevent unit conflation\n  measurement_basis TEXT,         -- e.g. 'irrigation_water_EC', 'nutrient_solution_EC', 'field_capacity_pct'\n  growth_stage    TEXT,           -- NULL = whole-cycle; else 'germination','vegetative', etc.\n  cultivar        TEXT,           -- NULL = all cultivars\n  cultivation_system TEXT,        -- NULL = all systems; else 'NFT','pot_subirrigation', etc.\n  source_id       TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source_citation TEXT NOT NULL,\n  notes           TEXT            -- verbatim caveats from the document\n);\n\n-- Dashboard-critical: explicit per-crop × axis coverage status\n-- This is what drives the UI card state (scored / advisory / monitor-only)\nCREATE TABLE axis_coverage (\n  crop_id         TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES crop(crop_id),\n  axis_id         TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sensor_axis(axis_id),\n  dashboard_tier  TEXT NOT NULL CHECK(dashboard_tier IN (\n    'scored',       -- direct evidence exists, numeric gauge possible\n    'advisory',     -- some evidence but category mismatch or scope-limited\n    'monitor_only'  -- no usable evidence; record telemetry, show guidance only\n  )),\n  evidence_statuses TEXT NOT NULL, -- JSON array of applicable statuses from gap registry vocabulary\n  reason_summary    TEXT NOT NULL, -- human-readable 1-line explanation for the UI tooltip\n  PRIMARY KEY (crop_id, axis_id)\n);\n\n-- Qualitative actions: section 9 content, always available even when no score exists\nCREATE TABLE qualitative_action (\n  action_id   INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n  crop_id     TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES crop(crop_id),\n  axis_id     TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sensor_axis(axis_id),\n  trigger_condition TEXT,  -- e.g. 'RH >= 85%', 'soil feels dry', NULL if general\n  action_text TEXT NOT NULL,\n  source_id   TEXT\n);\n\n-- Example axis_coverage rows showing the dashboard tier decision:\n-- INSERT INTO axis_coverage VALUES\n--   ('basil','air_temp','scored','[\"none\"]','Literature optimum 25-30C with cultivar trial support'),\n--   ('basil','air_humidity','advisory','[\"no_direct_evidence\"]','No growth-optimum RH; disease-risk thresholds (85%, 95%) available as context'),\n--   ('basil','illuminance_lux','monitor_only','[\"measurement_not_transferable\"]','Lux cannot be converted to documented PPFD/DLI without spectrum calibration'),\n--   ('basil','co2','monitor_only','[\"no_direct_evidence\"]','Only one interaction study; no per-crop optimum or threshold'),\n--   ('basil','soil_moisture','advisory','[\"measurement_not_transferable\"]','Field-capacity ratios exist but do not map to capacitive sensor readings'),\n--   ('basil','soil_temp','advisory','[\"stage_specific\"]','Germination and Pythium-management values only; no whole-cycle optimum'),\n--   ('basil','particulate_matter','monitor_only','[\"no_direct_evidence\"]','No horticultural threshold in any source'),\n--   ('basil','noise','monitor_only','[\"no_direct_evidence\"]','Not a recognized crop growth factor');\n\n-- Query the dashboard needs: 'what do I show for basil right now?'\n-- SELECT sa.display_name, ac.dashboard_tier, ac.reason_summary,\n--        eb.value_type, eb.range_low, eb.range_high, eb.unit,\n--        qa.action_text\n-- FROM sensor_axis sa\n-- JOIN axis_coverage ac ON ac.axis_id = sa.axis_id AND ac.crop_id = 'basil'\n-- LEFT JOIN evidence_band eb ON eb.axis_id = sa.axis_id AND eb.crop_id = 'basil'\n-- LEFT JOIN qualitative_action qa ON qa.axis_id = sa.axis_id AND qa.crop_id = 'basil'\n-- ORDER BY CASE ac.dashboard_tier WHEN 'scored' THEN 1 WHEN 'advisory' THEN 2 ELSE 3 END;","scorable_axes":["air_temperature — basil has literature-cited 25-30C optimum and chilling-injury threshold below 12C; lettuce has 18-24C facility range and 26.7C quality-risk line; strongest sensor-evidence alignment across all 8 crops","soil_temperature — germination-stage ranges exist for most crops (basil 23.9-29.4C, lettuce 12.8-18.3C) enabling stage-gated scoring when growth stage is known"],"unscorable_axes":["air_humidity — documented RH values are disease-risk thresholds (85%, 95%) not growth optima; scoring humidity against these would be a category error producing false alarms","illuminance_lux — all evidence is in PPFD/DLI; lux-to-PPFD conversion is spectrum-dependent and explicitly forbidden by the documents' own principles","CO2 — only one basil CO2-interaction study exists across all 8 crops; no per-crop optimum or threshold","particulate_matter — zero horticultural evidence in the corpus","noise — not a recognized crop growth factor; scoring it would be pseudoscience","soil_moisture — documented values use field-capacity ratios or system-specific VWC that are explicitly flagged measurement_not_transferable for generic capacitive sensors"],"assumptions":["Users are hobbyist indoor/pot growers who value actionable care tips over numeric precision — a different audience (researchers) would need a different UI","The 8 hardware sensors are fixed and no additional sensors will be added before MVP","Section 9 qualitative actions are complete enough to serve as the fallback content for advisory and monitor-only cards","The axis_coverage tier assignment will be manually curated during extraction, not auto-derived, which is acceptable at 8 crops × 8 axes = 64 rows"],"risks":["A three-tier dashboard where only 2 of 8 cards are fully scored may still feel empty and disappoint users expecting a single environment score","Qualitative guidance from section 9 is written for Korean-speaking gardeners and needs translation/adaptation for UI cards — effort not budgeted","The advisory tier is a UX grey zone: showing disease-risk humidity numbers without labeling them as non-optima risks misleading users despite correct schema modeling","axis_coverage rows are hand-curated judgments that embed product decisions in the database — if the curator conflates value_types, the same evidence-fidelity violation occurs at a different layer"],"cheap_validation":"Enumerate all 8 crops × 8 sensors (64 cells) and for each cell classify dashboard_tier as scored/advisory/monitor_only by checking the actual markdown for direct evidence. Count: if fewer than 12 cells are 'scored' across the entire matrix, the dashboard concept needs a fundamentally different design (e.g., guidance-first rather than gauge-first).","change_mind_if":"If the 64-cell enumeration shows that 3 or fewer crop×sensor pairs qualify as 'scored', even air temperature, the dashboard-with-gauges concept is not viable and the product should pivot to a pure guidance/checklist interface with telemetry graphs but no numeric scoring at all."}
